@startuml
title Phase 6 Sequential Evaluation And Checkpointing

skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Maintainer
participant "scripts.run_evaluation" as CLI
participant "evaluation.runner" as Runner
participant "Target client" as Target
participant "LocalLLMJudge" as Judge
participant "Judge model server" as JudgeServer
database "data/evaluation/<run>" as Output

Maintainer -> CLI: run_evaluation(config, run ID, model label)
CLI -> Runner: run_evaluation(args)
Runner -> Runner: load and validate benchmark
Runner -> Runner: fingerprint complete case content
Runner -> Target: initialize endpoint or prediction replay
Runner -> Judge: initialize separate local judge

loop each case, strictly sequential
  Runner -> Target: generate(case, target messages)
  Target --> Runner: candidate prediction
  Runner -> Judge: score(case, prediction)
  Judge -> JudgeServer: answer key + rubric + acceptable variants
  JudgeServer --> Judge: JSON verdict
  Judge -> Judge: validate score, reason, criteria, variant index
  alt invalid verdict and retry remains
    Judge -> JudgeServer: correction prompt with validation error
    JudgeServer --> Judge: corrected JSON verdict
  end
  Judge --> Runner: CaseScore
  Runner -> Output: atomically replace predictions.jsonl
  Runner -> Output: atomically replace case_results.jsonl
  Runner -> Output: atomically replace scores.json
  Runner -> Output: atomically replace evaluation_manifest.json
  note right of Output
    Files are replaced individually,
    not as one transaction.
    Manifest is the final commit marker;
    reconcile case IDs after interruption.
    in_progress until final case
    complete only after final verdict
  end note
end

Runner --> CLI: overall normalized score
CLI --> Maintainer: completion summary

note right of CLI
  Comparison fingerprints benchmark + judge,
  not target prompt/generation settings.
  A failed regression gate is written to JSON
  but comparison still exits 0.
end note

@enduml
